{"alignments": [{"id": "PSA.140.9.a001", "note": "*As for* stands before a fronted phrase carrying no object marker and no preposition, so no morpheme licenses it (rule 16); one unit, headed on *As* under rule 24.", "source": [], "source_head": null, "status": "added", "target": ["t001", "t002"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "PSA.140.9.a002", "note": "Construct noun with the supplied *the* rule 29 allows it.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.140.9.001"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.140.9.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003", "t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "PSA.140.9.a003", "note": "Rectum takes the relational *of* (rule 19) and, as an anarthrous participial substantive, the supplied *those that* (rule 46); *about* completes the English phrasal verb (rule 44), and the head is the word carrying the lexeme.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.140.9.002"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.140.9.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005", "t006", "t007", "t008", "t010"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "PSA.140.9.a004", "note": "Object suffix on the participle (rule 18).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.140.9.003"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.140.9.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "PSA.140.9.a005", "note": "Construct noun with the supplied *the* rule 29 allows it.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.140.9.004"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.140.9.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012", "t013"], "target_head": "t013"}, {"id": "PSA.140.9.a006", "note": "Rectum takes the relational *of* (rule 19), discontinuous around the possessive.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.140.9.005"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.140.9.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t014", "t017"], "target_head": "t017"}, {"id": "PSA.140.9.a007", "note": "Emphatic possessive: *their own* belongs whole to the suffix, headed on *their* (rule 18).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.140.9.006"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.140.9.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t015", "t016"], "target_head": "t015"}, {"id": "PSA.140.9.a008", "note": "Jussive verb takes the volitive frame *Let ... cover* (rule 17), discontinuous under rule 25 and headed on the lexical verb.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.140.9.007"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.140.9.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011", "t018"], "target_head": "t018"}, {"id": "PSA.140.9.a009", "note": "Object suffix.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.140.9.008"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.140.9.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t019"], "target_head": "t019"}], "ref": "PSA.140.9", "review_notes": ["The packet's ketiv/qere unit WLC.PSA.140.9.v001 is underdetermined with the base reading retained and its fallback still permitted by the English, so rule 53 does not arise."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": [{"base_source_ids": ["WLC.PSA.140.9.007", "WLC.PSA.140.9.008"], "compatible_readings": ["r00-base", "r01"], "evidence": "ASV 140:9 reads 'Let the mischief of their own lips cover them.' The qere yekassemo (3ms piel with suffix) and the ketiv yekassumo (3mp) differ only in the number of the covering verb; English 'Let ... cover them' is uninflected after 'let', so the rendering shows nothing of the verb's number, and the singular subject 'mischief' is the same collective noun under either reading. No ASV note is mapped to this unit. Underdetermined; the qere base fallback carries the projection.", "fallback_used": true, "operational_reading": "r00-base", "projected_source_ids": ["WLC.PSA.140.9.007", "WLC.PSA.140.9.008"], "ref": "PSA.140.9", "selected_reading": null, "status": "underdetermined", "unit_id": "WLC.PSA.140.9.v001"}]}
