coals] upon them'), which the ASV does not render: it supplies no agent dropping the coals. The verse's only note, 'Or, floods', is classed alternative_rendering and attaches to the English wording of mahamoroth, so it does not bear on this unit.", "fallback_used": false, "operational_reading": "r00-base", "projected_source_ids": ["WLC.PSA.140.10.001"], "ref": "PSA.140.10", "selected_reading": "r00-base", "status": "selected", "unit_id": "WLC.PSA.140.10.v002"}]}
{"alignments": [{"id": "PSA.140.11.a001", "note": "`אִישׁ לָשׁוֹן` is rendered by the single lexicalized expression *An evil speaker*, of which no morpheme owns a part (rule 30, read as one rendering rather than one token); the indefinite article belongs to the nominal expression under rule 15, and the source head is the governing construct (rule 23). The ASV's own Hebrew gloss *A man of tongue* corroborates and decides nothing (rule 38).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.140.11.001", "WLC.PSA.140.11.002"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.140.11.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001", "t002", "t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "PSA.140.11.a002", "note": "Negative particle.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.140.11.003"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.140.11.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "PSA.140.11.a003", "note": "Niphal with its auxiliary and copula (rule 17), discontinuous around the negative.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.140.11.004"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.140.11.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004", "t006", "t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "PSA.140.11.a004", "note": "Preposition.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.140.11.005"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.140.11.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "PSA.140.11.a005", "note": "Assimilated article takes the written *the* (rule 12).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.140.11.006"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.140.11.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "PSA.140.11.a006", "note": "Noun.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.140.11.007"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.140.11.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "PSA.140.11.a007", "note": "Anarthrous substantival adjective standing as the clause's subject; the ASV writes it bare (rule 46).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.140.11.010"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.140.11.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "PSA.140.11.a008", "note": "Finite verb with auxiliary (rule 17).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.140.11.011"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.140.11.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012", "t013"], "target_head": "t013"}, {"id": "PSA.140.11.a009", "note": "Chain rendered attributively; the supplied determiner is the construct noun's (rules 28-29).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.140.11.008"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.140.11.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t014", "t016"], "target_head": "t016"}, {"id": "PSA.140.11.a010", "note": "Rectum rendered attributively.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.140.11.009"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.140.11.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t015"], "target_head": "t015"}, {"id": "PSA.140.11.a011", "note": "Preposition rendered *to* before the recast verbal noun.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.140.11.013"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.140.11.013", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t017"], "target_head": "t017"}, {"id": "PSA.140.11.a012", "note": "Noun recast as an English verb.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.140.11.014"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.140.11.014", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t018"], "target_head": "t018"}, {"id": "PSA.140.11.a013", "note": "Object suffix; the ASV realizes it once, as the object of the recast *overthrow* (rule 18), the fronted `אִישׁ־חָמָס` keeping its own English.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.140.11.012"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.140.11.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t019"], "target_head": "t019"}], "ref": "PSA.140.11", "review_notes": ["The object suffix of `יְצוּדֶנּוּ` was given the final *him* rather than the noun phrase *the violent man*, which answers to the written `אִישׁ חָמָס`; counting the ASV's pronouns against the morphemes that could carry them leaves no word unaccounted either way."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "PSA.140.12.a001", "note": "Finite verb with its subject pronoun (rule 17).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.140.12.001"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.140.12.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001", "t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "PSA.140.12.a002", "note": "Complementizer.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.140.12.002"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.140.12.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "PSA.140.12.a003", "note": "Finite verb with auxiliary (rule 17).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.140.12.003"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.140.12.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005", "t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "PSA.140.12.a004", "note": "Divine name as subject.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.140.12.004"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.140.12.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "PSA.140.12.a005", "note": "Construct noun with the supplied *the* rule 29 allows it.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.140.12.005"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.140.12.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007", "t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "PSA.140.12.a006", "note": "Rectum takes the relational *of* (rule 19); the anarthrous substantival adjective takes the supplied *the* under rule 46.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.140.12.006"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.140.12.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009", "t010", "t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "PSA.140.12.a007", "note": "Coordinator written for a colon in which no conjunction morpheme stands (rule 14's closing sentences); it is not folded into the noun beside it.", "source": [], "source_head": null, "status": "added", "target": ["t012"], "target_head": "t012"}, {"id": "PSA.140.12.a008", "note": "Construct noun; the ASV writes no determiner for it.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.140.12.007"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.140.12.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t013"], "target_head": "t013"}, {"id": "PSA.140.12.a009", "note": "Rectum takes the construct relation recast as *for* (rule 1